  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The identified factors and their rankings rely on retrospective participant interviews in two Swedish cities, which may reflect localized institutional structures and subjective recall.",
      "what": "Through a mixed-methods approach, this study traced participant insights across two Swedish cities from 1960 to 2024 using interviews to identify 40 factors shaping stormwater management transitions. These elements were synthesized into 9 key factors and ranked by participants, revealing that external collaboration is perceived as the most critical factor for future sustainable stormwater management.",
      "why": "The study demonstrates that these key decision factors function as dynamic, adaptive levers rather than static barriers or drivers, shifting in influence across time and space to offer a transferable framework that challenges purely technical and economic decision paradigms."
